# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# board_sim (tools/) is a HOST development tool -- a Unicorn-based CPU emulator
# built with clang on macOS/Linux, not cross-compiled target firmware. The
# following MISRA-C:2012 rules are deviated for it because they are inherent to
# the host-tool role and the Unicorn callback ABI it is built on, not defects:
#   21.6  -- it is a CLI tool; <stdio.h> IS its interface (printf/fopen/...).
#   21.3  -- host tool; malloc/free for framebuffers is appropriate (no P10).
#   11.x  -- Unicorn's hook/MMIO ABI passes user data as void* and installs
#            handlers via function-pointer casts; both are unavoidable.
#   15.5  -- guard-clause early returns are the house style (advisory).
#   17.7  -- some libc / Unicorn return values are intentionally ignored.
# See docs/qualification/MISRA_DEVIATIONS.md (D-BSIM) for the rationale. These
# scope to tools/board_sim only; every other MISRA rule is still enforced there,
# so a genuine defect (e.g. an uninitialised read) is still reported.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
misra-c2012-21.6:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-21.3:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-11.1:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-11.2:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-11.3:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-11.5:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-11.6:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-11.8:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-15.5:tools/board_sim/*
misra-c2012-17.7:tools/board_sim/*

